# STATE: Current Execution Pointer (template)

Spec: StateFile

Purpose:
  Compact current-state pointer for the /sdd-next resolver. This is
  the FIRST file /sdd-next reads — the AI never re-analyzes the full
  SDD tree to discover what is next (token economy [I3], chat §13).

Owns: templates/specdd/state.template.sdd

Location (instance):
  projects/{project_name}/.specdd/state/current.sdd

Rules:
  [SF1] /sdd-next reads STATE FIRST; falls back to scanning
        decisions/tasks ONLY when STATE is missing or stale.
  [SF2] The resolver updates STATE after every completed unit.
  [SF3] STATE is DERIVED data — never a second source of truth.
        On conflict, project files (decisions/, tasks/) WIN and
        STATE is rebuilt from them.

Fields:

  current_decision: DEC-<ID>
      The decision currently being delivered.

  current_task: TASK-<ID>
      The task currently executing under the current decision.

  current_subtask: SUBTASK-<ID>
      The unit currently resolved (or next TODO unit).

  status: <SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE state>
      Lifecycle state of current_subtask.

  last_completed:
    - SUBTASK-<ID>
      Recently closed units (most recent first; older entries pruned
      by /sdd-compact).

  updated: <timestamp>
      Last resolver update — staleness signal for [SF1] fallback.

Template body (copy into the instance):

  current_decision: DEC-000
  current_task: TASK-000
  current_subtask: SUBTASK-TASK-000-00
  status: TODO
  last_completed: []
  updated: <iso-8601>

Navigation:
  NextCommand: @../../commands/sdd-next.sdd
  SubtaskStateMachine: @../../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  SubtaskSchema: @../../schemas/subtask.sdd
  DeliveryState: @../../chains/delivery.sdd (StepState — separate,
    per-run delivery step state; STATE points at units, StepState
    at delivery steps; they never duplicate each other)

State: +
  (Phase 155: created as the read-first token-economy pointer for
   /sdd-next --subtask resolution)
